646,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.10408553697520297,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":52.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.1577345806139823,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.18141477018457985,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":93.8,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.07309440744287876,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":61.5,"_gate_margins":0.006398034276769682,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":56.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0.008800067511500193,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":8.8,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04524919520497428,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":61.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0555117295894485,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007839335342816684,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.08971,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":59.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Laureate Education, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, offers higher education programs and services to students through a portfolio of higher education institutions in Mexico, Peru, and the United States. The company offers a range of undergraduate, graduate, and specialized degree programs in the areas of medicine and health sciences, engineering and information technology, and business and management through campus-based, online, and hybrid programs. It also operates universities and technical-vocational institutions, as well as provides high school education services. The company was formerly known as Sylvan Learning Systems, Inc. and changed its name to Laureate Education, Inc. in May 2004. Laureate Education, Inc. was founded in 1989 and is headquartered in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eilif  Serck-Hanssen | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 33K people. Revenue per employee of $50K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, with revenue falling 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $8K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $394 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 52\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Laureate Education, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $4.8B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $263M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 9.0% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $21.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Laureate (NASDAQ:LAUR) Tests A Long-Term Line: Ready To Rise?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/laureate-nasdaqlaur-tests-a-long-term-line-ready-to-rise","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794495780.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(LAUR) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily